  "notes": "USAGE:\nTakes a direct object with を marking the action the person is reluctant to do. Often used in the ～ている form to describe an ongoing state of reluctance. Related to the adjective {渋|しぶ}い, sharing the root meaning of something being difficult or unpleasant.\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {返事|へんじ}を{渋|しぶ}る: to be reluctant to answer\n- {支払|しはら}いを{渋|しぶ}る: to be reluctant to pay\n- {協力|きょうりょく}を{渋|しぶ}る: to be reluctant to cooperate\n- {許可|きょか}を{渋|しぶ}る: to be reluctant to grant permission",
